-- title:
--   Frobenius read-off at an unramified prime, up to the cubic partner
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$; let $\Phi$ be a Hecke eigensystem over $\mathbb{Q}$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$ (a level together with coefficient functions $a,b$ on the height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$), let $i\in\{0,1\}$, let $\ell$ be a prime, and let $Q$ be a prime ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ with finite residue field lying over $\ell\mathbb{Z}$ whose inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ is trivial. Write $\iota=$ [`AutomorphicForm.iotaZsqrtdNegTwo`](def/AutomorphicForm_ViaCompactCuspNotion.html#L15) for the embedding $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]\to\mathbb{C}$ sending $\sqrt{-2}$ to $\sqrt{2}\,i$, write $\Phi_i$ for $\Phi$ when $i=0$ and for the twist of $\Phi$ by $v\mapsto\iota(\chi_{-3}(v))$ (so $a\mapsto\chi a$, $b\mapsto\chi^2 b$) when $i=1$, and for a subgroup $H\le\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ write $\mathrm{seed}_H$ for the $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$-valued eigensystem of level $\top$ over the fixed field of $H$ whose $a$- and $b$-entries at $w$ are the trace and the determinant of the explicit lift `liftOf` of $e$ applied to the relative Frobenius power `seedFrob` at $w$. Two hypotheses are imposed. First, for every height-one prime $w$ of the fixed field of $\ker(\det\circ e)$ lying under the rational prime $\ell$, the $b$-entry at $w$ of the formal base change of $\Phi$ (namely $\Phi.b(\ell)$ raised to the residue degree of $w$) equals $\iota$ of the $b$-entry of $\mathrm{seed}_{\ker(\det\circ e)}$ at $w$. Second, for every height-one prime $u$ above $\ell$ in the fixed field of the project's subgroup [`LanglandsTunnell.sylowH e`](def/LanglandsTunnell_SylowH.html#L17) (the $\gamma$ whose image $e(\gamma)$ is the mod-$3$ reduction, under $\mathrm{red}:\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]\to\mathbb{Z}/3$, $\sqrt{-2}\mapsto -1$, of a matrix in the project's set `P16`), both entries of the formal base change of $\Phi_i$ at $u$ (Satake power and power of $b$ in the residue degree) agree with $\iota$ of the corresponding entries of $\mathrm{seed}_{\mathrm{sylowH}(e)}$ at $u$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a matrix $M$ in the multiplicative monoid generated by the two explicit matrices [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Slift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L21) and [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Tlift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L23) over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ such that: the entrywise reduction of $M$ by $\mathrm{red}$ is the matrix $e(\mathrm{Frob}_Q)$; $\Phi_i.b(\ell)=\iota(\det M)$; and either $\Phi_i.a(\ell)=\iota(\operatorname{tr}M)$, or else no prime $u$ above $\ell$ in the fixed field of $\mathrm{sylowH}(e)$ has residue degree $1$ and $\Phi_i.a(\ell)=\iota(-2\operatorname{tr}M)$.
--
--   This is the local read-off step in the octahedral case of the Langlands–Tunnell argument: it recovers the Hecke data of the chosen face of $\Phi$ at an unramified rational prime $\ell$ from what is visible after formal base change to the quadratic resolvent field and to the fixed field of the $2$-Sylow subgroup, with the trace determined only up to the alternative $-2\operatorname{tr}M$ coming from the other root of the relevant cubic. It is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow_of_coversModCentre`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow_of_coversModCentre) and [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_of_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_of_agreesLiftTraceSeed_isCusp_pair).
